cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference this study, cite the repository record below."
title: "News alpha in crypto: a complete study"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible study of whether public news and macro releases can be traded
  profitably in crypto at realistic costs and realistic latency. 86,171 headlines
  from 11 sources form 45,625 (headline, symbol) pairs on Binance one-minute bars,
  plus 714 spot listings, 923 perpetual listings, 528 macro releases and 1,040
  minute-level shocks. Eleven of twelve tested ideas lose money after costs; CPI
  releases at 60 minutes remain a candidate, not a strategy. Includes nine
  documented defects that were found and fixed, and an independent verifier that
  recomputes every published number without importing the pipeline.
authors:
